# ai_tools_dotnet file contexts: the .NET output layout inside a SANDBOX CLONE. Clones are labelled by the static rule
# in ai_tools.fc plus a plain restorecon (no per-clone semanage rule, no root), so the build-output directories inside
# one need a static rule of their own, and it lives in the integration's layout module because the names are
# the integration's: the same set as the type transitions in ai_tools_dotnet.te, which states the coupling. Written
# under both /opt and /var/opt for the same reason the clone rule in ai_tools.fc is: the `/var/opt /opt` path alias is
# in EL10's file_contexts.subs_dist and not in EL9's, so each host reaches one of the pair. A claimed project
# under a home gets the equivalent rule per project from relabel.lib.sh, from the same names in the manifest.
#
# Precedence: each rule here and the clone rule in ai_tools.fc under the same prefix share a stem (the literal prefix
# before the first metacharacter), and among equal stems the later, longer regex is the match, so a path under bin/,
# obj/ or artifacts/ resolves here and every other clone path to the clone rule. Verify on a host with the module
# loaded, since this is the property the narrowing rests on:
#   matchpathcon /var/opt/ai-tools/sandbox-projects/x/src/p/bin/y   (expect ai_tools_project_build_t)
#   matchpathcon /var/opt/ai-tools/sandbox-projects/x/.githooks/h   (expect ai_tools_project_t)
/opt/ai-tools/sandbox-projects/[^/]+(/.*)?/(bin|obj|artifacts)(/.*)?      gen_context(system_u:object_r:ai_tools_project_build_t,s0)
/var/opt/ai-tools/sandbox-projects/[^/]+(/.*)?/(bin|obj|artifacts)(/.*)?  gen_context(system_u:object_r:ai_tools_project_build_t,s0)
